From de6dd6a57eb0c312020e2f0a8c74e6c4c5e0d394 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 06:03:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(update): a gateway that defers three updates in a row
 gets a repair card [daveey]

The 2026-11-11 hub wall (eleven updates deferred by one gateway that could never take
the idle pause) left one log line per attempt and no owner. The pre-swap pause now
keeps a streak per refusing gateway (update-pause-deferrals.<install>.json beside the
pause record): PauseRefused carries the gateway names, a pause that goes through ends
every streak, and a deferral naming another gateway starts over. From the third
consecutive deferral naming the same gateway, update_pause_deferrals files one Kanban
card (idempotent per install + gateway, filed in a fresh interpreter like
update_upstream_conflict; an open card is kept and re-commented every 12th deferral,
a finished one is replaced). Bookkeeping never changes the update's verdict.
